[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite.py: Implemented interface module: added @data_type decorators to all data types, @operation to Protocol methods, @singleton_type to DAG/WaveScheduler/DAGRunner, fixed exception classes (removed frozen=True), added __str__ methods to exception classes, removed prohibited [slug:...] contract references from docstrings.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_pretense.py: Implemented complete Pretense state machine for DAG, WaveScheduler, and DAGRunner interfaces. Fixed import to use package-qualified path (benchmark_1.parts.dag_engine_lite.lib.dag_engine_lite). Replaced all Domain.required placeholders with concrete Domain.type() strategies. Replaced all _unimplemented_transition stubs with inner_transition() calls using concrete return values (NodeDefinition, Set[str], List[str], bool, DAGRunReport, etc.). Added List import, module-level _dummy_action function to avoid lambdas, and fixed fake factory function signature.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Implemented implementation pseudo-state machine and real test suite for DagEngineLite. Fixed all bare parts imports to use package-qualified paths (benchmark_1.parts.dag_engine_lite.*). Replaced self.fail placeholder with concrete test methods covering add_node, add_edge, remove_node, has_node, get_node, dependencies/dependents, all_nodes, validate, topological_sort, find_roots/leaves, compute_critical_path, wave scheduler operations, failure policies, and full DAGRunner run. Moved SUT class to module level to resolve PRE_LINT_NO_PRE_SEEDING loop violation. Added collaborators tracking for Hypothesis fuzzing.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Implemented concrete classes: DAG (node management, cycle detection, topological sort, critical path), WaveScheduler (wave scheduling, state management, failure policies), DAGRunner (sequential wave execution with retries and failure handling). All three singletons registered properly.
